course: dictionary
lesson: 10722
title: Unworthy and the clues around it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unworthy means not good enough to deserve something, or not fit for someone's good character. You can work out its meaning from the words around it. «I felt unworthy of the prize.» If you feel unworthy of a prize, you do not feel you deserve it.
explain: Look at this sentence: «The Badger looked at him very suspiciously, but Toad's frank, open countenance made it difficult to suggest any unworthy motive.» Toad looked honest and open, so it was hard to think he had a bad reason. An unworthy motive is a reason that is not good enough. Check it by swapping in "bad reason": it still makes sense.
explain: «That mean comment is unworthy of you.» Here unworthy means the comment is not good enough for you, so the speaker is gently telling you off. Notice that unworthy is often followed by "of".
fact: Unworthy means not deserving something, or not good enough for someone's character.
fact: Useful phrases: «feel unworthy», «unworthy of», «unworthy of attention».
fact: «Countenance» means face, and «motive» means the reason for doing something.
fact: In church language, people may say they are unworthy before God, which means they need God's mercy.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «I felt unworthy of the prize.» What does unworthy mean here? | Late for the prize-giving | *Not deserving the prize | Very proud and happy | Shiny and golden
exercise: «Toad's frank, open countenance made it difficult to suggest any unworthy motive.» Which word means face? | suggest | open | frank | *countenance
exercise: «That mean comment is unworthy of you.» What does unworthy suggest here? | *The comment is not good enough for you | You deserve a prize | The comment is very funny | The comment was a whisper
test: «The hero felt unworthy at first, but later proved himself.» What does unworthy mean? | *Did not feel good enough to deserve it | Brave and loud | Lost in the woods | Very happy and proud
test: In «Toad's face was open and honest, so no unworthy motive was suggested», what is a motive? | *A reason for doing something | A type of face | A kind of hat | A loud noise
exam: Which sentence uses unworthy correctly? | «He felt unworthy of the bright sunshine.» | «He felt unworthy to be a sandwich.» | «He felt unworthy of the number seven.» | *«He felt unworthy of such kindness.»
